# Supabase

Jachai uses Supabase for **auth**, **Pro entitlement**, and **planned bKash checkout** — not for articles/clusters (those live in backend PostgreSQL).

## Layout

- `supabase/config.toml` — local CLI project (`project_id = "jachai-news"`, Postgres 15)
- `supabase/migrations/` — versioned SQL; initial migration: `20250301000000_init_profiles_subscriptions.sql`
- Frontend types: `frontend/src/lib/database.types.ts` — **keep in sync** when migrations change

## Apply schema

- Linked project: `supabase db push`
- Or paste migration SQL into the Supabase dashboard SQL editor
- Local dev: `supabase start` then `supabase db reset` / push as needed

Regenerate TS types after schema changes:

```bash
npx supabase gen types typescript --local > frontend/src/lib/database.types.ts
```

(Use `--project-id` for remote when not using local.)

## Tables & enums

| Object | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `public.profiles` | One row per `auth.users`; `locale` `en` \| `bn`; auto-created via `handle_new_user` trigger |
| `public.subscriptions` | One row per user (`user_id` unique); `subscription_plan` monthly/yearly; `subscription_status` trialing/active/past_due/canceled/expired |
| `public.bkash_agreements` | Tokenized checkout agreement IDs per user (planned) |
| `public.payment_transactions` | bKash (default provider) charges linked to `subscription_id`; `metadata` jsonb |

## Row Level Security

- RLS enabled on all four public tables
- **Anon/authenticated users**: SELECT own rows only (`auth.uid()` = `id` or `user_id`); users may UPDATE own `profiles`
- **No client INSERT** on subscriptions, agreements, or payments — writes are for **service role** (Edge Functions, server route with `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`), not `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`

## Frontend wiring

- Client: `frontend/src/lib/supabase.ts` — `createClient<Database>(...)` when URL + anon key are set in `.env.local`
- Entitlements (not wired yet): read `subscriptions` where `status` in (`active`, `trialing`) and `current_period_end` > now; until then `hasProAccess()` in `subscription-access.ts` uses `NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO`
- Pricing/feature copy stays in `subscription-plans.ts` and `subscription-features.ts` (not in DB)

## Migrations conventions

- One logical change per migration file; timestamp prefix `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_name.sql`
- Prefer explicit RLS policies and comments on tables intended for service-role writes
- Do not store news/RSS/cluster data here; do not commit service role keys or bKash secrets
